// spec: a global of the program named as one of the standard library's function templates (`empty`, Iterator.kpp) is a name clash, the one error, and no code is generated: lookup takes the name as one of them, so whatever followed was the clash's echo
// factorio: from D's value corpus: `int empty` gave "static assertion whose condition the compiler cannot evaluate yet" and a codegen error beside the clash
// error: global_named_as_library_function_template_is_error.kpp:5: error: 'empty' is declared here and in the standard library
// error: top-level name(s) declared twice: no code generated
constexpr int empty = 3;
static_assert(empty == 3, "empty is the global");
int main()
{
  println("{}", empty);
  return 0;
}
